<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karang Brahi inscription</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 7th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Karang Brahi inscription is a Srivijayan stone inscription in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-malay">Old Malay</a>, found in 1904 on the upper Merangin river in Jambi, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>. Undated, it is usually placed close to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kota-kapur-inscription">Kota Kapur inscription</a> of 686 because its curse formula is almost the same. It records <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a>'s authority over the Jambi region, the former heartland of the Melayu kingdom.</p></div>
